  "title": "EXPON.DIST and EXPONDIST stage t = RN53(RN64(lambda * x)) with subnormal flush on t and outputs",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 builds 20131, 20430, and 20527, EXPON.DIST and EXPONDIST require x >= 0 and lambda > 0, compute t = RN53(RN64(lambda * x)) flushing subnormal t to 0, return -expm1(-t) when cumulative is TRUE and RN53(RN64(lambda * EXP(-t))) when cumulative is FALSE, and flush subnormal outputs to 0 (e.g. EXPON.DIST(1E-300, 1E-10, TRUE) = 0). All 4,934 EXPON.DIST and 1,196 EXPONDIST full-bank rows match.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in Excel 16.0.20527.20088 (dc96l3_discrete rows 189-206, 228) and CalcFunc-Evidence runs/w111-extended-numeric-20260929/answers/answers-expon.dist.json.gz and answers-expondist.json.gz (Excel 16.0 build 20430); 4,934/4,934 EXPON.DIST and 1,196/1,196 EXPONDIST full-bank rows match.",
